NNAAMMEE
     qqaatt__cc22xxxxxx — Intel QuickAssist Technology (QAT) driver for Atom C2000
     chipsets

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ccrryyppttoo
           ddeevviiccee ccrryyppttooddeevv
           ddeevviiccee qqaatt

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following lines in loader.conf(5):

           qat_c2xxx_load="YES"
           qat_c2xxxfw_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The qqaatt__cc22xxxxxx driver implements crypto(4) support for some of the crypto‐
     graphic acceleration functions of the Intel QuickAssist (QAT) device
     found on Atom C2000 devices.  QAT devices are enumerated through PCIe and
     are thus visible in pciconf(8) output.

     The qqaatt__cc22xxxxxx driver can accelerate AES in CBC, CTR, and GCM modes, and
     can perform authenticated encryption combining the CBC, and CTR modes
     with SHA1-HMAC and SHA2-HMAC.  The qqaatt__cc22xxxxxx driver can also compute SHA1
     and SHA2 digests.  The implementation of AES-GCM has a firmware-imposed
     constraint that the length of any additional authenticated data (AAD)
     must not exceed 240 bytes.  The driver thus rejects crypto(9) requests
     that do not satisfy this constraint.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     crypto(4), ipsec(4), pci(4), qat(4), random(4), crypto(7), crypto(9)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The qqaatt__cc22xxxxxx driver first appeared in FreeBSD 13.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The qqaatt__cc22xxxxxx driver was written for NetBSD by Hikaru Abe
     <_h_i_k_a_r_u_@_i_i_j_._a_d_._j_p>.
     Mark Johnston <_m_a_r_k_j_@_F_r_e_e_B_S_D_._o_r_g> ported the driver to FreeBSD.

BBUUGGSS
     Some Atom C2000 QAT devices have two acceleration engines instead of one.
     The qqaatt__cc22xxxxxx driver currently misbehaves when both are enabled and thus
     does not enable the second acceleration engine if one is present.

